Qore krb5 module

INTRODUCTION
------------
The Qore krb5 module provides Kerberos 5 and GSSAPI primitives for Qore.

This initial implementation provides:
- Kerberos default realm and credential-cache helpers
- Kerberos credential metadata and cache store/list helpers
- Kerberos default keytab and keytab entry-management helpers
- in-memory credential-cache initialization for tests and service setup
- filesystem sandbox enforcement for file-backed credential caches
- filesystem sandbox enforcement for file-backed keytabs
- Kerberos principal parsing and introspection
- GSSAPI initiator target-name handling
- GSSAPI context stepping with hex-encoded tokens

The module is designed as the security foundation for enterprise LDAP and
Active Directory integrations on Linux.

BUILDING
--------
Requires qore 2.0+ and MIT Kerberos / GSSAPI development libraries.

CMake build:
  mkdir build && cd build
  cmake .. -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug
  cmake --build .

To run the local tests from the repo root:
  test/run-tests.sh

